<title>INDIA: India details rail freight rises for key goods.</title>
<headline>India details rail freight rises for key goods.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Railway Board chairman M.K. Kaw on Wednesday detailed the estimated increases in freight charges for key commodities from a 12 percent rise in rates announced in the railway budget for 1997/98 (April-March).</p>
<p>Following are the estimated increases:</p>
<p>    Coal			   45 rupees per tonne</p>
<p>    High-speed diesel	  9.19 paise per litre</p>
<p>    Petrol			 8.45 paise per litre</p>
<p>    Cement			 2.45 rupees per 50 kg</p>
<p>($1 = 35.8 rupees) (1 rupee = 100 paise)</p>
<p>- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
